{"content": "1|# Workstation Testing
2|
3|A Workstation change is stable only when its **behavioral contract** is proven at the lowest useful layer and the relevant integration path remains green. Typecheck or source-shape checks alone are not proof.
4|
5|## Validation ladder
6|
7|Use the smallest focused gate first, then expand only after it passes:
8|
9|1. **Pure/unit behavior** — extracted logic, state transitions, serialization, routing decisions, host/geometry helpers.
10|2. **Workstation contracts** — `workstation/tests/` for Python-side routing/config/integration contracts.
11|3. **Desktop UI tests** — renderer behavior through Vitest/React tests when UI state or actions change.
12|4. **Desktop platform tests** — Electron/main-process behavior for `WebContentsView`, BrowserRuntime, host ownership, persistence, and IPC contracts.
13|5. **Desktop typecheck/build gates** — ensure changed contracts compile across renderer/preload/main boundaries.
14|6. **Windows Desktop E2E/smoke** — required for claims that depend on real Electron/Windows composition, restart, profile persistence, or native view geometry.
15|
16|Do not replace an executable behavior test with a test that greps `.py`, `.ts`, or `.tsx` source text. Follow the root `AGENTS.md` testing rules. Source-shape tests are acceptable only for build/bootstrap policy (for example proving that an installer does not invoke a mutator); they are not substitutes for runtime behavior tests.
17|
18|## Existing Workstation gates
19|
20|- `Workstation CI`
21|  - component lock validation;
22|  - third-party license validation;
23|  - `workstation/tests/`;
24|  - downstream integration-anchor check in read-only `--check` mode.
25|- `Workstation Browser Windows`
26|  - Node/Python setup;
27|  - read-only committed-integration validation;
28|  - normal `workstation\\install.cmd` execution;
29|  - a clean-checkout assertion after install;
30|  - Desktop typecheck;
31|  - Desktop UI tests;
32|  - Desktop platform/Electron tests;
33|  - a final outcome aggregator that keeps the job red if either broad Desktop suite fails.
34|- `tests/tui_gateway/test_workstation_browser_schema_capability.py`
35|  - focused regression gate for Desktop Browser schema ownership;
36|  - proves Desktop capability survives a false reachability probe;
37|  - proves Desktop tool-definition cache state cannot leak into TUI;
38|  - proves a process-global `HERMES_DESKTOP` flag cannot grant TUI capability;
39|  - proves Desktop source identity is sufficient without that process env flag;
40|  - proves the forced Workstation set stays narrow (`browser_exec` is not promoted).
41|- `apps/desktop/electron/workstation-browser-task.test.ts`
42|  - pure BrowserTask lifecycle/persistence contract;
43|  - proves `hide` and `park` preserve the same page and current URL;
44|  - proves `destroy` is explicit;
45|  - proves only one logical record exists per task;
46|  - proves switching the visible task parks the previous task semantically;
47|  - proves malformed/duplicate persisted metadata is pruned;
48|  - proves restart restoration is parked and page recovery is lazy.
49|- `apps/desktop/electron/workstation-browser-runtime-task.test.ts`
50|  - exercises the lifecycle adapter against the real `WorkstationBrowserRuntime` with Electron mocked, without Browserless/network access;
51|  - proves `ownerTaskId` is idempotent in the Chromium tab primitive;
52|  - proves hide/park/show retain the same `WebContents` and URL within one process;
53|  - proves explicit task destroy closes the owned page;
54|  - proves restart restores task metadata first and creates one task-owned page only when shown again.
55|
56|The Windows workflow must test the **committed tree**. Migration/patch helpers must not repair source before these tests run. A clean clone followed by normal install must remain clean according to `git status`, apart from deliberately ignored artifacts such as `.venv`, `node_modules`, caches, and runtime state outside the checkout.
57|
58|The UI and platform/Electron steps are intentionally independent after typecheck: each may record a failed outcome while allowing the other suite to run, then the final aggregator fails the job if either outcome is not `success`. This is **diagnostic non-masking**, not failure tolerance; no coverage is disabled and a red suite still makes the workflow red.
59|
60|## Session-scoped capability test policy
61|
62|A GUI/browser surface capability must be tested as a **session contract**, not by mutating a process-global environment variable and observing a single process-wide cache. Focused tests should bind `gateway.session_context`, exercise schema assembly with reachability forced false, and then switch surface identity within the same process to prove cache isolation.
63|
64|The forced-schema path may only preserve a schema that is already selected by the active toolsets; it must never re-add a disabled/unselected tool. Runtime health, recovery, bound-task fail-closed behavior, and fallback policy remain execution-time responsibilities and need their own tests.
65|
66|## BrowserTask lifecycle test policy
67|
68|BrowserTask tests must distinguish **logical task persistence** from **process-local page identity**:
69|
70|- within one Electron process, `create -> hide -> show` and `create -> park -> show` must retain the same live page object and current URL;
71|- `hide`/`park` must not close the `WebContents`;
72|- an explicit `destroyTask` is the operation that removes the task and closes its owned page;
73|- repeated creation for the same `taskId` must not allocate a second live page;
74|- if a page crashes/disappears while the logical task remains, recovery may create exactly one replacement and must record that recovery;
75|- after Desktop process restart, task metadata must restore as parked before any page is recreated; showing/using that task may lazily recreate one page under the same `taskId`;
76|- tests must never claim that a JavaScript heap or `WebContents` object itself survives a process restart.
77|
78|Use the pure lifecycle test first, then the runtime-adapter test, then the Windows Desktop gate. Browserless/network access is unnecessary for these lifecycle invariants.
79|
80|## Baseline comparison for pre-existing failures
81|
82|When a broad gate is already red on `main` and blocks causality for a narrowly scoped change, reproduce the exact `main` base and the candidate with the same OS image, toolchain, dependency install, and commands. Compare failure signatures rather than only failure counts. A baseline/candidate A/B may establish that a failure is pre-existing and that the scoped change is non-regressive, but it must not be described as a green broad gate.
83|
84|Record the base SHA, candidate SHA, run IDs, failing files/tests or error classes, and any runner-only flake. Keep the permanent gate red until the underlying issue is fixed; do not add allowlists that silently convert known failures into success unless a separately justified test architecture explicitly requires it.
85|
86|## Required browser-foundation invariants
87|
88|As the corresponding implementation lands, tests must establish these relationships rather than freeze incidental values:
89|
90|- a GUI/Desktop session receives its browser surface capability independently of process env identity;
91|- controller reachability affects execution/recovery, not whether the valid session surface is known to the model;
92|- a BrowserTask can hide/show/park/focus without creating a replacement live page;
93|- destroy is explicit and different from hide;
94|- task-bound controller loss is fail-closed;
95|- routing-disabled stays internal-only;
96|- Chat Browser View and Browser Hub reference the same BrowserTask/runtime;
97|- only one host owns the live `WebContentsView` at a time;
98|- host transfer/resize updates bounds without overlap;
99|- multiple BrowserTasks remain isolated;
100|- BrowserSessionState restoration preserves safe logical metadata without storing credentials;
101|- Chromium profile persistence is tested separately from logical tab/task restoration;
102|- Preview compatibility in Workstation mode does not create a second independent browser lane;
103|- `web_search` remains available for factual non-UI research while explicit visible/authenticated browser work exposes the Workstation Browser contract.
104|
105|## Manual Windows smoke evidence
106|
107|For behavior Electron automation cannot reliably prove, record a reproducible smoke procedure and result. The browser foundation's final smoke must cover at least:
108|
109|1. start a cleanly installed Desktop build;
110|2. start a browser task from Chat;
111|3. observe the same task in Chat Browser View and Browser Hub;
112|4. interact through agent control, then Take Control as a human on the same page;
113|5. hide and reopen without a new navigation;
114|6. switch Chat ↔ Browser Hub and resize/maximize/restore without native-view overlap;
115|7. create a second task and verify isolation;
116|8. restart Desktop and verify logical tabs/task mappings restore;
117|9. separately verify compatible login state persists through the dedicated Chromium profile;
118|10. exercise controller loss for a bound task and verify fail-closed behavior.
119|
120|Implementation 4's narrower lifecycle smoke may be recorded before the Chat/Hub surfaces exist, but it must at minimum prove on a real Windows Desktop process that a task-owned page can be created/navigated, hidden or parked, re-exposed without a replacement navigation, explicitly destroyed, and logically restored after restart. Missing later-surface steps must remain listed as future work rather than being marked passed by the narrower smoke.
121|
122|Record the exact commit SHA, Windows/Node/Python versions, commands/workflow run, observed result, and any limitation. A manual pass on an unidentifiable build is not durable evidence.
123|
124|## Failure policy
125|
126|A red gate is investigated, not disabled. If a pre-existing failure blocks validation, reproduce it, identify whether it is in scope, and either fix it in the narrowest appropriate implementation or record why a different existing gate provides sufficient proof for the scoped change. Never make CI green by deleting coverage for the behavior being changed, and never turn a baseline-equivalent failure into a claimed pass.", "total_lines": 125, "file_size": 10005, "truncated": false, "is_binary": false, "is_image": false}

{"content": "1|import fs from 'node:fs'
2|import path from 'node:path'
3|
4|export const BROWSER_TASK_STATE_VERSION = 1
5|
6|export type BrowserTaskStatus = 'visible' | 'hidden' | 'parked'
7|export type BrowserTaskRecoveryState = 'fresh' | 'restored' | 'recreated' | null
8|
9|export interface BrowserTask {
10|  taskId: string
11|  createdAt: string
12|  panelHost: string | null
13|  controlHost: string | null
14|  sessionHost: string | null
15|  localConnection: string | null
16|  status: BrowserTaskStatus
17|  leaseState: string | null
18|  parked: boolean
19|  recoveryState: BrowserTaskRecoveryState
20|  updatedAt: string
21|}
22|
23|export interface BrowserTaskSnapshot {
24|  version: typeof BROWSER_TASK_STATE_VERSION
25|  browserTaskCounter: number
26|  tasks: BrowserTask[]
27|}
28|
29|export interface BrowserTaskSeed {
30|  taskId?: string
31|  panelHost?: string | null
32|  controlHost?: string | null
33|  sessionHost?: string | null
34|  localConnection?: string | null
35|  leaseState?: string | null
36|}
37|
38|export interface BrowserTaskBindings<Page, ShowContext = void> {
39|  ensurePage(taskId: string): Page
40|  pageForTask(taskId: string): Page | null
41|  pageIsAlive(page: Page): boolean
42|  showPage(taskId: string, page: Page, context: ShowContext): void
43|  hidePage(taskId: string, page: Page): void
44|  parkPage(taskId: string, page: Page): void
45|  destroyPage(taskId: string, page: Page): void
46|}
47|
48|export interface BrowserTaskPersistence {
49|  load(): BrowserTaskSnapshot | null
50|  save(snapshot: BrowserTaskSnapshot): void
51|}
52|
53|function cloneTask(task: BrowserTask): BrowserTask {
54|  return { ...task }
55|}
56|
57|function validText(value: unknown): value is string {
58|  return typeof value === 'string' && value.trim().length > 0
59|}
60|
61|function validNullableText(value: unknown): value is string | null {
62|  return value === null || typeof value === 'string'
63|}
64|
65|function validStatus(value: unknown): value is BrowserTaskStatus {
66|  return value === 'visible' || value === 'hidden' || value === 'parked'
67|}
68|
69|function validRecoveryState(value: unknown): value is BrowserTaskRecoveryState {
70|  return value === null || value === 'fresh' || value === 'restored' || value === 'recreated'
71|}
72|
73|function parsePersistedTask(value: unknown): BrowserTask | null {
74|  if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return null
75|  const task = value as Partial<BrowserTask> & { status?: unknown; recoveryState?: unknown }
76|  if (!validText(task.taskId) || !validText(task.createdAt) || !validText(task.updatedAt)) return null
77|  if (!validStatus(task.status) || !validRecoveryState(task.recoveryState)) return null
78|  if (!validNullableText(task.panelHost) || !validNullableText(task.controlHost)) return null
79|  if (!validNullableText(task.sessionHost) || !validNullableText(task.localConnection)) return null
80|  if (!validNullableText(task.leaseState) || typeof task.parked !== 'boolean') return null
81|
82|  return {
83|    taskId: task.taskId.trim(),
84|    createdAt: task.createdAt,
85|    panelHost: task.panelHost,
86|    controlHost: task.controlHost,
87|    sessionHost: task.sessionHost,
88|    localConnection: task.localConnection,
89|    status: task.status,
90|    leaseState: task.leaseState,
91|    parked: task.parked,
92|    recoveryState: task.recoveryState,
93|    updatedAt: task.updatedAt
94|  }
95|}
96|
97|export function normalizeBrowserTaskSnapshot(value: unknown): BrowserTaskSnapshot | null {
98|  if (!value || typeof value !== 'object') return null
99|  const snapshot = value as { version?: unknown; browserTaskCounter?: unknown; tasks?: unknown }
100|  if (snapshot.version !== BROWSER_TASK_STATE_VERSION) return null
101|  if (!Number.isInteger(snapshot.browserTaskCounter) || Number(snapshot.browserTaskCounter) < 0) return null
102|  if (!Array.isArray(snapshot.tasks)) return null
103|
104|  // One logical task may appear only once. If a crash left duplicate metadata,
105|  // keep the most recently updated valid record and discard the stale duplicate.
106|  const deduped = new Map<string, BrowserTask>()
107|  for (const raw of snapshot.tasks) {
108|    const parsed = parsePersistedTask(raw)
109|    if (!parsed) continue
110|    const current = deduped.get(parsed.taskId)
111|    if (!current || parsed.updatedAt >= current.updatedAt) deduped.set(parsed.taskId, parsed)
112|  }
113|
114|  return {
115|    version: BROWSER_TASK_STATE_VERSION,
116|    browserTaskCounter: Number(snapshot.browserTaskCounter),
117|    tasks: [...deduped.values()]
118|  }
119|}
120|
121|export class BrowserTaskFilePersistence implements BrowserTaskPersistence {
122|  constructor(readonly filePath: string) {}
123|
124|  load(): BrowserTaskSnapshot | null {
125|    try {
126|      return normalizeBrowserTaskSnapshot(JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(this.filePath, 'utf-8')))
127|    } catch {
128|      return null
129|    }
130|  }
131|
132|  save(snapshot: BrowserTaskSnapshot): void {
133|    fs.mkdirSync(path.dirname(this.filePath), { recursive: true })
134|    const temp = `${this.filePath}.${process.pid}.${Date.now()}.tmp`
135|    fs.writeFileSync(temp, JSON.stringify(snapshot, null, 2), { encoding: 'utf-8', mode: 0o600 })
136|    fs.renameSync(temp, this.filePath)
137|    try {
138|      fs.chmodSync(this.filePath, 0o600)
139|    } catch {
140|      // Best effort on Windows / filesystems without POSIX permissions.
141|    }
142|  }
143|}
144|
145|export class BrowserTaskLifecycle<Page, ShowContext = void> {
146|  private readonly tasks = new Map<string, BrowserTask>()
147|  private browserTaskCounter = 0
148|
149|  constructor(
150|    private readonly bindings: BrowserTaskBindings<Page, ShowContext>,
151|    private readonly persistence: BrowserTaskPersistence | null = null,
152|    private readonly now: () => Date = () => new Date()
153|  ) {}
154|
155|  restore(): BrowserTask[] {
156|    const snapshot = this.persistence?.load()
157|    if (!snapshot) return []
158|
159|    this.tasks.clear()
160|    this.browserTaskCounter = snapshot.browserTaskCounter
161|    const timestamp = this.timestamp()
162|    for (const saved of snapshot.tasks) {
163|      // Renderer/WebContents identity cannot survive an Electron process restart.
164|      // Preserve logical ownership, but normalize the task to parked metadata and
165|      // lazily recreate/recover its page only when the task is shown or used.
166|      this.tasks.set(saved.taskId, {
167|        ...saved,
168|        status: 'parked',
169|        parked: true,
170|        recoveryState: 'restored',
171|        updatedAt: timestamp
172|      })
173|    }
174|    this.persist()
175|    return this.listTasks()
176|  }
177|
178|  createTask(seed: BrowserTaskSeed = {}): BrowserTask {
179|    const taskId = seed.taskId?.trim() || `browser-task-${++this.browserTaskCounter}`
180|    const existing = this.tasks.get(taskId)
181|    if (existing) {
182|      this.ensureLivePage(taskId, existing)
183|      return cloneTask(existing)
184|    }
185|
186|    const timestamp = this.timestamp()
187|    const task: BrowserTask = {
188|      taskId,
189|      createdAt: timestamp,
190|      panelHost: seed.panelHost ?? null,
191|      controlHost: seed.controlHost ?? null,
192|      sessionHost: seed.sessionHost ?? null,
193|      localConnection: seed.localConnection ?? null,
194|      status: 'parked',
195|      leaseState: seed.leaseState ?? null,
196|      parked: true,
197|      recoveryState: 'fresh',
198|      updatedAt: timestamp
199|    }
200|    this.tasks.set(taskId, task)
201|    this.bindings.ensurePage(taskId)
202|    this.persist()
203|    return cloneTask(task)
204|  }
205|
206|  showTask(taskId: string, context: ShowContext): BrowserTask {
207|    const task = this.requireTask(taskId)
208|    const timestamp = this.timestamp()
209|    let parkedOther = false
210|    for (const other of this.tasks.values()) {
211|      if (other.taskId === taskId || other.status !== 'visible') continue
212|      const otherPage = this.livePage(other.taskId)
213|      if (otherPage) this.bindings.parkPage(other.taskId, otherPage)
214|      Object.assign(other, { status: 'parked' as const, parked: true, updatedAt: timestamp })
215|      parkedOther = true
216|    }
217|    if (parkedOther) this.persist()
218|
219|    const page = this.ensureLivePage(taskId, task)
220|    this.bindings.showPage(taskId, page, context)
221|    return this.updateTask(task, { status: 'visible', parked: false })
222|  }
223|
224|  hideTask(taskId: string): BrowserTask {
225|    const task = this.requireTask(taskId)
226|    const page = this.livePage(taskId)
227|    if (page) this.bindings.hidePage(taskId, page)
228|    return this.updateTask(task, { status: 'hidden', parked: false })
229|  }
230|
231|  parkTask(taskId: string): BrowserTask {
232|    const task = this.requireTask(taskId)
233|    const page = this.livePage(taskId)
234|    if (page) this.bindings.parkPage(taskId, page)
235|    return this.updateTask(task, { status: 'parked', parked: true })
236|  }
237|
238|  destroyTask(taskId: string): boolean {
239|    const task = this.tasks.get(taskId)
240|    if (!task) return false
241|    const page = this.livePage(taskId)
242|    if (page) this.bindings.destroyPage(taskId, page)
243|    this.tasks.delete(taskId)
244|    this.persist()
245|    return true
246|  }
247|
248|  task(taskId: string): BrowserTask | null {
249|    const task = this.tasks.get(taskId)
250|    return task ? cloneTask(task) : null
251|  }
252|
253|  listTasks(): BrowserTask[] {
254|    return [...this.tasks.values()].map(cloneTask)
255|  }
256|
257|  snapshot(): BrowserTaskSnapshot {
258|    return {
259|      version: BROWSER_TASK_STATE_VERSION,
260|      browserTaskCounter: this.browserTaskCounter,
261|      tasks: this.listTasks()
262|    }
263|  }
264|
265|  private requireTask(taskId: string): BrowserTask {
266|    const task = this.tasks.get(taskId)
267|    if (!task) throw new Error(`BrowserTask not found: ${taskId}`)
268|    return task
269|  }
270|
271|  private livePage(taskId: string): Page | null {
272|    const page = this.bindings.pageForTask(taskId)
273|    return page && this.bindings.pageIsAlive(page) ? page : null
274|  }
275|
276|  private ensureLivePage(taskId: string, task: BrowserTask): Page {
277|    const existing = this.livePage(taskId)
278|    if (existing) return existing
279|    const page = this.bindings.ensurePage(taskId)
280|    if (!this.bindings.pageIsAlive(page)) throw new Error(`BrowserTask page could not be recovered: ${taskId}`)
281|    task.recoveryState = 'recreated'
282|    task.updatedAt = this.timestamp()
283|    this.persist()
284|    return page
285|  }
286|
287|  private updateTask(task: BrowserTask, patch: Pick<BrowserTask, 'status' | 'parked'>): BrowserTask {
288|    Object.assign(task, patch, { updatedAt: this.timestamp() })
289|    this.persist()
290|    return cloneTask(task)
291|  }
292|
293|  private persist(): void {
294|    this.persistence?.save(this.snapshot())
295|  }
296|
297|  private timestamp(): string {
298|    return this.now().toISOString()
299|  }
300|}
