{"content": "1|/**
2| * Hermes Workstation Browser Runtime
3| *
4| * First-class Chromium runtime hosted inside Hermes Desktop. Electron already
5| * ships Chromium, so Workstation does not require Chrome/Edge as a product
6| * dependency.
7| *
8| * The runtime deliberately has two control surfaces over ONE WebContentsView
9| * pool:
10| *   1. Electron IPC for the Browser page the human sees.
11| *   2. A loopback-only bearer-authenticated controller for Hermes browser_*
12| *      tools and Kanban workers. The controller file is user-local and never
13| *      exposed on LAN.
14| *
15| * Browser tabs survive route changes and continue in the background. Task ids
16| * are bound to tabs so a background worker never steals the user's active tab.
17| * Once a task owns an internal tab, recovery is expected to reconnect to this
18| * runtime rather than silently moving the task to a different browser.
19| *
20| * The attach/detach + lifecycle design is adapted from browser-use/desktop's
21| * BrowserPool (MIT). See workstation/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
22| */
23|
